&lt;p&gt;We’re scaling fast and staying true to what makes us different: an open-source legacy, a global collaborative culture, and a passion for meaningful work. Our team thrives in an innovation-driven environment where transparency, autonomy, and trust fuel everything we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may not meet every requirement, and that’s okay. If this role excites you, we’d love you to raise your hand for what could be a truly career-defining opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grafana Labs is looking for a technically fluent engineer who loves building powerful demos, explaining complex systems clearly, and helping SRE and platform engineering leaders understand the value of our open approach to observability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Grafana’s offering shifts from dashboards to industry-leading agentic observability, our Product Marketing team is responsible for closing the gap between what our products can do and how customers understand that value. That means building clear, consistent positioning, enabling sellers with trustworthy technical narratives, and creating content that helps Platform Engineering teams quickly grasp why Grafana Cloud is the right choice for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Product Marketer you will play a critical part in that transformation. You’ll be the hands-on engineer who brings our technical story to life for buyers, not just practitioners. You’ll build core demos, run technical workshops and webinars, and act as the technical bridge between our Product and Sales orgs. Your work will help SRE and platform engineering leaders evaluate Grafana with confidence, equip sales engineers with better tools and talk tracks, and ensure our technical value shows up clearly and consistently across the entire customer journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique chance to shape how Grafana tells its story as we evolve our positioning in the AI era, strengthen seller enablement, and build a repeatable system for communicating product value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build strategic, buyer-focused demos, videos, workshops, and webinars&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain polished, narrative-driven demos that highlight Grafana’s value for SRE and platform engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Record high-quality technical demo videos and walkthroughs in partnership with our video and content teams.

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is the trusted source for open source. By delivering hardened, secure, and production-ready builds of all the open source software engineers and AI agents rely on, Chainguard helps organizations build faster, stay compliant, and eliminate risk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our customers include Fortune 500 enterprises and global industry leaders, including Anduril, Canva, Fortinet, Hewlett Packard Enterprise, OpenAI, Snap Inc., and Snowflake. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Chainguard is venture-backed by leading investors, including Amplify, IVP, Kleiner Perkins, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Mantis VC, Redpoint Ventures, Sequoia Capital, and Spark Capital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Product Security Researcher&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: US, Canada, UK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imagine a world where we’re not just reacting to the latest security headline, but shaping the future threat landscape so our customers sleep better at night (and so do we).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Principal Product Security Researcher&lt;/strong&gt; at Chainguard, you’ll lead our product security research function end-to-end: mapping emerging threats, turning insight into strategy, and helping Chainguard stay several moves ahead of attackers across our entire product portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role, in a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chainguard prioritizes our customers’ security above all else, which means preparing not just for the attacks of today, but for those of tomorrow as well. In this Principal-level role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product security research agenda for Chainguard scanning the broader ecosystem, identifying emerging attack patterns, and translating them into clear risks and opportunities for Chainguard and our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape security direction across products and platforms, partnering closely with Product, Engineering, and Security leadership to embed your findings into roadmaps, architecture decisions, and long-term plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the agenda and discussion topics across the whole industry, helping everyone to understand what is important, where the risks are, and why they should pay attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy turning ambiguous, fast-moving threat intel into concrete, multi-quarter plans that change how a company operates, this is your playground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research emerging threats &amp;amp; trends in software supply chain and product security, and analyze their impact on Chainguard’s products and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design creative mitigations across people, process, and technology into pragmatic defenses that actually get adopted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with executive and senior engineering leadership to drive org-level security strategy, influence key roadmap decisions, and secure buy-in for big, complex changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systematic weaknesses (in systems, structures, and sometimes habits) and develop plans that fix root causes in ways that persist long after you’ve moved on to the next hard problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and uplevel others across Product Security and Engineering by helping teams think more strategically about threats, risk, and long-term security posture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take input and suggestions from across the organisation, balancing various stakeholders, and delivering value for different functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Chainguard externally through talks, conferences, and thought leadership, sharing what we’re learning and helping move the industry forward.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt; &amp;nbsp;If using AI for your resume or

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chainguard is the trusted source for open source. By delivering hardened, secure, and production-ready builds of all the open source software engineers and AI agents rely on, Chainguard helps organizations build faster, stay compliant, and eliminate risk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our customers include Fortune 500 enterprises and global industry leaders, including Anduril, Canva, Fortinet, Hewlett Packard Enterprise, OpenAI, Snap Inc., and Snowflake. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Chainguard is venture-backed by leading investors, including Amplify, IVP, Kleiner Perkins, Lightspeed Venture Partners, Mantis VC, Redpoint Ventures, Sequoia Capital, and Spark Capital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Product Security Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role, in a nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Chainguard, our security posture is our competitive advantage. In this principal‑level role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set product security direction across major products and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multi‑quarter, cross‑functional security initiatives that materially reduce risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed security by design into roadmaps and day‑to‑day engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate with high autonomy, working directly with engineering and product leadership to turn high‑level risk into concrete, shippable plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape product security strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Define and evolve security guardrails for AI-assisted development from design and coding through testing, review, deployment and operations so teams can move quickly while using AI responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead large‑scale security initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Own cross‑functional programs (e.g., secure SDLC improvements, vulnerability reduction) that span multiple teams and quarters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate vulnerability remediation and automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Partner with engineering to build automation for vulnerability detection, triage, and remediation (including STIGs/CIS baselines and policy‑as‑code), shortening time‑to‑fix for critical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve security assurance programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Improve how we run and consume pentests, vulnerability assessments, bug bounty programs, and red‑team activity so findings become lasting engineering and process changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion secure‑by‑default tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Guide adoption and integration of security tools (static/dynamic analysis, dependency and license checks, IaC scanners) into CI/CD in a way that works with, not against, developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
