&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Helping clients&amp;nbsp;identify&amp;nbsp;and explore where AI and automation could add value,&amp;nbsp;shaping&amp;nbsp;practical use cases and supporting early adoption&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Anduril Australia we are developing unmanned systems for subsurface and other domains that will leverage unsupervised autonomy for the delivery of long endurance, multi-mission capability to our customers. These projects, including but not limited to the Extra Large Autonomous Undersea Vehicle (XL-AUV) Program, require Mechanical Engineers with broad experience to drive the delivery a variety of software enabled hardware capabilities to our customers. Anduril Mechanical Engineers rapidly develop expertise in new domains in order to architect, design, deliver, support, and evolve next generation capabilities through the entire product life-cycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating detailed plans and specifications for new designs, or derivatives of the Anduril Extra Large Autonomous Undersea Vehicles (XL-AUVs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating detailed mechanical designs, prototypes and build of complex structures and mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simulation and analysis of mechanical designs including modal/spectral response analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all designs meet internal and external maritime standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert for your areas of expertise as they relate to the delivery of Anduril technology capabilities, including areas such as part design, analysis and material selection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspecting parts, sub-systems and vehicles to meet design specifications and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement integrated systems, including advanced and sensitive platforms and payloads, that rapidly delivers capability beyond the scope of current systems, with a clear path for both architecture and capability evolution over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathise with end-users and drive solutions that balance their needs with external constraints, restrictions and requirements in a multi-stakeholder environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design and development of technology components across Anduril, with the aim of developing components that are re-usable across multiple Anduril product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design, implementation and execution of development processes for the initial delivery and subsequent iteration of structural hardware, including full lifecycle testing, monitoring and operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support vehicle and payload manufacturing, testing and deployment. Including DVT (Design Validation Testing) of parts and sub systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to co-locate with end-users, vendors, or the integration and test team up to 20% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work as a member of a multi-disciplinary engineering team, including as a mentor for more Junior Engineers from differing backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace, Naval Architecture, a relevant field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience working as a Mechanical Engineer with one or more domains and/or technologies o

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The UK Growth team owns how Anduril builds and converts opportunity in the UK, from market engagement and capture through to contract. We draw on business lines, legal, finance, engineering, programme management expertise from across Anduril to turn capability into contracts. There is no dedicated commercial function in the UK today. This role is the first of its kind, sitting within Growth, and the person in this seat will shape Anduril UK’s commercial approach.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a Commercial Officer to join our rapidly growing team in London. You will own and drive the commercial strategy for Anduril&#39;s UK defence business, operating at the intersection of strategy, business development, and deal execution. You will help build and manage a pipeline of government and defence contracts, structure and negotiate deals, and make sure Anduril captures and delivers on opportunities across the MOD.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role demands breadth. You will engage at senior levels with military leaders, government officials, and industry partners, and you will also roll up your sleeves on contract negotiation, pricing, and bid strategy. Anduril&#39;s UK presence is scaling fast and established playbooks for all scenarios do not yet exist, so you must be comfortable with ambiguity and willing to build process where none exists.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute Anduril&#39;s commercial strategy for the UK defence market, aligned with the company&#39;s growth objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the wider Business Development team to win opportunities across UK government procurement programmes, direct contracts, and partnership-led bids.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop pricing and margin strategy in coordination with business lines and Global Defence, balancing competitiveness with business sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deal structuring, negotiation, and close on major defence contracts, including government-to-government, prime-sub, and teaming arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the commercial terms of bids and proposals, ensuring alignment with MOD procurement frameworks (e.g. DEFCON, SSRO regulations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage commercial risk across the portfolio, including export control compliance (ITAR/EAR), offset/industrial participation obligations, and sovereign requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary commercial interface with MOD Commercial and Defence Procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and sustain relationships at senior levels across UK MOD, the NADG, and Front Line Commands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Anduril at industry events, defence exhibitions, and government engagements as a credible commercial voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Anduril&#39;s US-based commercial and legal teams to align UK deal structures with corporate standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the UK commercial function from the ground up – hiring, process, negotiating, deal structuring&lt;/li&gt;
