&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(40, 40, 40);&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Our leading SaaS-based Global Employment Platform™ enables clients to expand into over 180 countries quickly and efficiently, without the complexities of establishing local entities. At G-P, we’re dedicated to breaking down barriers to global business and creating opportunities for everyone, everywhere.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Our diverse, remote-first teams are essential to our success. We empower our Dream Team members with flexibility and resources, fostering an environment where innovation thrives and every contribution is valued and celebrated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The work you do here will positively impact lives around the world. We stand by our promise: Opportunity Made Possible. In addition to competitive compensation and benefits, we invite you to join us in expanding your skills and helping to reshape the future of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(40, 40, 40); font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;At G-P, we assist organizations in building exceptional global teams in days, not months—streamlining the hiring, onboarding, and management process to unlock growth potential for all.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Field Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt;, you will join a high-performing team laser-focused on taking over the market, building a world-class company, and solving the complex international expansion needs of thousands of employers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this full-cycle outbound role, you will lead the charge in driving new logo acquisition across the EMEA region. We are looking for relentless hunters who excel at multi-threaded deal execution, master modern prospecting frameworks, and leverage cutting-edge AI tools to maximize their impact. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment and have a deep desire to win, this is your opportunity to build a high-growth sales career at the recognized leader in Employer of Record (EoR).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Targeted Outbound Prospecting:&lt;/strong&gt; Execute a sophisticated multi-channel prospecting motion (phone, email, social selling, video, etc.) to build a robust, high-quality pipeline across target EMEA accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-Threaded Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Build strategic relationships across prospect organizations—from key operational champions up to economic buyers and C-level executives—aligning our solutions with their top-level business initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver the G-P Value Proposition:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a domain expert on global hiring, articulating the strategic, financial, and operational benefits of G-P as the premier global Employer of Record (EoR) provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Cycle Deal Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead complex sales cycles from initial cold outreach to discovery, solution mapping, commercial proposal generation, objection handling, and deal closure against monthly targets.&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Since 2004, we’ve been bringing investment ideas to life and connecting capital with the right people and opportunities. Today, we manage more than £2.5 billion for a broad range of investors across five key investment strategies: Private Credit,&amp;nbsp;Social Housing, Clean Heat, Energy and Venture. These strategies underpin the innovative range of investments we offer to both private (retail) and institutional clients.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There are 230+ employees at Triple Point, all committed to leaving the world demonstrably better than we found it. That’s why we’re a certified B Corp, signed up to the Principles for Responsible Investment, and were named a Sunday Times &lt;em&gt;&#39;Best Place to Work&amp;nbsp; 2025 &amp;amp; 2026&#39;&lt;/em&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;f this sounds like an environment where you would flourish, then read on…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table style=&quot;width: 819px;&quot; width=&quot;642&quot;&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;width: 804.219px;&quot; width=&quot;642&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Function &amp;amp; Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our purpose is to ensure that Triple Point operates in strict adherence to the rules and regulations established by the FCA. It’s our duty to diligently monitor industry standards and incorporate best practices throughout the organisation. A crucial part of our mission is to enhance awareness and understanding of the financial regulations that directly impact our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining the GRC function, you will become part of a collaborative and professional team that plays an essential role in supporting the firm’s success. Your contributions will directly influence how the business protects the personal data entrusted to it, while providing you with broad exposure to the firm’s operations, systems and third-party relationships. This is an opportunity to strengthen Triple Point’s control environment and to play a meaningful role in sustaining the company’s long-term resilience and reputation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style=&quot;width: 804.219px;&quot; width=&quot;642&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data Privacy Analyst will play a crucial part in ensuring Triple Point’s day-to-day business processes, structure and operations adhere to UK data protection frameworks, including the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018 (DPA 2018).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Data Protection Officer (DPO), the role provides dedicated capacity for the GDPR enhancement programme, tracked against the ten pillars of the Group’s Accountability Tracker, and takes on a growing share of business-as-usual privacy activity. It works closely with Compliance, Digital &amp;amp; Technology, Legal, People and Client Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone with a positive attitude who embraces problem-solving and enjoys collaborating with teams across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk assessments: support the completion of Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) and Transfer Impact Assessments (TIAs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data inventory and data governance: support the business to complete system and information data-flow mapping, including supporting Digital &amp;amp; Technology with the Information Asset Register.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Records and retention: help develop and maintain the Record of Processing Activities (ROPA) and the Data Retention Schedule, providing guidance and support to senior personnel within the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rights and request resolution: help develop the subject access rights process and procedure, and handle data subjec

&lt;p&gt;Convene Hospitality Group (CHG) operates a global portfolio of lifestyle brands focused on creating places and experiences that bring people together. The company designs, develops, and operates hospitality-driven destinations to host gatherings of all kinds, ranging from small corporate meetings to immersive brand activations and beyond. We love bringing people together in person, and that passion for great experiences extends to our employees as well. If you&#39;re interested in creating inspiring moments of connection, consider joining our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior AR Analyst, Credit Control | London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note: candidate must currently reside in the UK and be able to work in the UK without sponsorship.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Convene Hospitality Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Convene Hospitality Group designs and operates experiential event venues, bringing premium meeting and event experiences to some of the world’s leading organisations. Through a growing portfolio of brands including Convene, etc.venues and NeueHouse, we operate a network of nearly 40 venues and are the largest single provider of dedicated meeting and event spaces across the US and UK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK is central to that story. From our Convene venues across the City of London to etc.venues in London and Manchester, and with our new West End destination, Convene Rathbone, our UK footprint continues to grow, and so does the pace of the events we deliver. Every conference, board meeting and live event our clients host relies on a finance team that keeps things moving behind the scenes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Senior Accounts Receivable (AR) Analyst, Credit Control to join our UK Finance team and help lead AR operations across our UK venue portfolio. Reporting to the AR Manager, you’ll take ownership of billing, credit control and cash allocation, turning client contracts and booking data into accurate, timely invoices, following up on outstanding balances, allocating customer receipts and keeping customer accounts clean and reconciled in our financial systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role with real visibility. You’ll work closely with Sales, Event Operations and client procurement teams, acting as a trusted partner who keeps cash flowing while protecting the strong client relationships our business is built on. For someone who brings both rigour and a commercial mindset, it’s an opportunity to make a direct impact on the financial health of a growing UK business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daily Operations &amp;amp; Cash Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare multi-bank reconciliation spreadsheets (Santander, JPM, Online Credit Cards) and resolve unapplied cash exceptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process incoming payments (ACH, credit cards, wires, cheques) and apply them accurately to customer accounts in NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Issue final invoices for standard customer accounts and review/process credit memos and billing adjustments with proper approvals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer record updates in NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Credit Control &amp;amp; Collections:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take direct ownership of chasing overdue accounts via calls, emails, and structured collection cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review the AR Aging report weekly to track overdue accounts, identify delinquent trends, and prioritise high-value collection efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate severely overdue or high-risk accounts to Finance/Sales Management

&lt;h2&gt;Opportunity &amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brunswick Group is seeking an enthusiastic and analytical Apprentice BI Data Analyst to join its Group Business Intelligence (BI) team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Group BI team plays a key role in supporting the business globally by delivering meaningful data, reporting and analysis to inform strategic decisions. Working closely with Finance, FP&amp;amp;A, the Commercial Hub and other business teams, the function develops and maintains reporting systems and BI dashboards, helping stakeholders better understand financial performance, revenue and recovery data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will work within the BI development team, reporting to the BI Technical Support Analyst. The role involves providing technical support, investigating and resolving reporting issues, and assisting with the development and improvement of dashboards to enhance self-service reporting across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alongside gaining hands-on experience with Microsoft Dynamics 365, Azure SQL Server and Power BI, the successful candidate will complete a Level 4 Data Analyst Apprenticeship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a motivated individual with strong analytical and interpersonal skills, a keen interest in data and technology, and a willingness to learn. Previous Business Intelligence experience is not required, as training and mentoring will be provided. Applicants must meet the apprenticeship eligibility requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your day-to-day responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily integrity checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating issues raised by end-users and resolve them or escalating them to the development team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide immediate solutions to system issues and liaise with other support teams to ensure prompt resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage small scale changes through to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality assurance tests and assisting with new release processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate and enhance workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and administer reporting security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with people across the firm to enable them to self-serve Business Intelligence through Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with developers to support the technical implementation and roll-out of new reporting dashboards on Power BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As skills and knowledge are gained, personally take on development work, through SQL and Power BI within the team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Brunswick, we seek smart and curious individuals dedicated to learning and growth. We value potential, strong work ethic, and excellent written and verbal communication skills. Standout candidates demonstrate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Excel, with an enthusiasm to develop more advanced skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in working with data and using it to solve business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate effectively with colleagues at all levels of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive approach and willingness to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A resilient, enthusiastic team player with strong self-motivation and a collaborative, hands-on approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in databases and data; previous exposure to SQL would be beneficial but is not essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in Business Intelligence and data visualisation; previous exposure to Power BI would be beneficial but is not essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in developing commercial and financial understanding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of fun&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications close on &lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Friday 30th October 2026 a

